# What never enters a build context.
#
# Docker does not read .gitignore, so nothing above this file protects a build
# from the working tree. Two specific hazards, both of which have bitten real
# projects and both of which fail quietly here:
#
# 1. `.env.local` is the documented way to run the conductor locally, so a
#    developer who has ever done that is carrying DATABASE_URL and the
#    RLS-bypassing SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY in a file sitting next to the
#    Dockerfile. `COPY apps/conductor apps/conductor` would bake both into a
#    readable image layer — recoverable with `docker history` long after the
#    file itself is gone — and the process would then read them at startup for
#    every variable the real env_file happens not to define.
#
# 2. `node_modules` on this machine is a pnpm symlink farm pointing at paths
#    that do not exist inside the image. Copying it over the freshly installed
#    tree replaces working dependencies with dangling links.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/node_modules
.git
.github
.turbo
**/.next
**/dist
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

# Not needed to run anything, and large.
design/prototypes
doc/archive
